Attribution — rule-name catalogue
---------------------------------

The check/rule name vocabulary used by this project — for example
`find_via_antennas`, `find_pads_center_not_connected`,
`find_orphan_net_labels`, `find_missing_decoupling`,
`find_designator_collisions`, and the general `find_*` style — is
adopted from the LINT_AUDIT_LIST catalogue in salitronic/eda-agent
(https://github.com/salitronic/eda-agent), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

We use their names deliberately so that anyone familiar with eda-agent
finds a recognisable vocabulary here. Rule implementations are
independent work: eda-agent drives live sessions of Altium, KiCad, or
EasyEDA Pro via an MCP server, whereas easyeda-lint parses EasyEDA
Standard JSON exports offline. No Apache-2.0 code from eda-agent is
redistributed in this project.

A copy of the Apache-2.0 license text is available at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.
